 "version": 1,
 "title": "EBM Stomp",
 "category": "Drums and grooves",
 "text": "Sound: a slow, heavy, stomping body-music beat: a booming kick like a boot on a factory floor every beat, a huge snare on 2 and 4 in a cavernous room, and a metallic clank on the off-beats. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: one Clock at 112. The kick with a longer, booming decay and a deeper drop. The snare, longer and fuller, on 2 and 4 from a Sequencer. The clank: two oscillators multiplied in a Ring Mod, struck by a short envelope from a second Sequencer on the off-beats. Everything mixed, driven, and put in a big Reverb.\n\nTweak: DRIVE, the reverb's SIZE, the clank oscillators' TUNE, TEMPO.",
